From 6d88fae0b31585608dfccc117af1b122a113e5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:44:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: buffer while a read waits for its source, and
 end with an error when it is given up

The thread of the player reads its packets and checks, between reads,
whether the audio and video players have run dry, when it buffers: the
clock stops until the queues fill again. While a read waits for its
source that check does not run: the picture stays still with no
explanation, the clock goes on, and once the data is back the players
race through what they missed.

Around each read of a packet the player now gives its input a function
(IOControl::READ_WAIT), which a read of a cached file of known length
calls while it waits for its source. It does what the loop would do when
the players have run dry (SetCaching(CACHESTATE_FULL): the clock stops,
the GUI shows the player caching) and nothing that seeks, flushes or
reads; a stop still ends the read at once (IOControl::READ_ABORT). After
5 s without data a notification says that the connection is interrupted
and that playback resumes by itself, again every 30 s, on any skin. When
the cache gives the source up (5 minutes without data, or a server that
refuses the file), the input reports it (SourceFailed()) and playback ends
with an error, which keeps the position, and a notification, instead of
as if the video had been played to its end.

New strings: core 39888, 39889, 39953; Estuary 31616 to 31618 (en_gb,
es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
